Z||000000||FieroGT||08-09-2000||02:45 PM||||Well, I finally found myself with such litle time on my hands that I must bring myself to sell my '85 SE-V6. Car has all GT bodywork on it, is still a notchback. No A/C, and second gear has become nonfunctional in the 4-spd tranny. Car runs great, has recent clutch, new GM master and slave, too. I just can't stand to let the car sit until I get a chance to find time for it. So far, it's been out of commission for 6 weeks, and I don't forsee having any time to spend on it until next spring. I've owned this car for about 9 years, now. And rather than let it rot, I'd much rather give someone crafty the opportunity to own one of there plastic wonders. It will be sad to see her go, though. I have many scars (literally!) that I can attribute to working on the car. But each time behind the wheel (even when it was my only car for a few years) I got a s**t-eating grin!<P>I've been notoriously absent from posting lately, but I always lurk around. I've watch this board grow from 50 members and am really pleased at how its turned out. Kudos to Cliff and to all of you for such a fine job here. <P>Just a little sad about getting rid of the SE and had to share, that's all. Thanks for the ear-time!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>John||||reg||9
